{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\user\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -LiteralPath \\\"C:\\\\Projects\\\\Agent_Workspace\\\\HG-KSEOS\\\\var\\\\swof-construction-002-w2\\\\specs\\\\W2_CORRECTIVE_CW2_SPEC.md\\\" -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# SWOF W2 CORRECTIVE CW2 SPEC — close the round-2 independent findings\n\nRound-2 independent adversarial verification on candidate `4469813c086b864cfd82383400a11ce2831b8433`\nconfirmed that all five round-1 counterexamples now HOLD and that no law regressed, but found one new\nBLOCKING bypass and four non-blocking gaps. You are the tracked mutation writer for corrective CW2.\nYou may write ONLY these paths:\n\n```\nsrc/assurance/oracle.py\nsrc/assurance/evidence.py\nsrc/assurance/journal.py\nsrc/assurance/README.md\nsrc/assurance/tests/test_oracle.py\nsrc/assurance/tests/test_evidence.py\nsrc/assurance/tests/test_journal.py\nsrc/assurance/tests/test_adversarial.py\nsrc/effect/idempotency.py\nsrc/effect/substrate.py\nsrc/effect/README.md\nsrc/effect/tests/test_idempotency.py\nsrc/effect/tests/test_adversarial.py\nsrc/security/classification.py\nsrc/security/tests/test_classification.py\nsrc/security/tests/test_adversarial.py\n```\n\nAny other path is a governance violation. Python 3.11+, stdlib ONLY, ASCII only, LF endings.\nDo not weaken or delete any existing assertion, and do not shrink any test count.\n\n## F1 (BLOCKING) — `src/assurance/oracle.py`: the negative-fixture law is still bypassable\n\nThe reviewer showed that `proven = bool(proof_kinds & present_kinds) or fixture in present_ids` lets an\nevidence item whose `item_id` merely EQUALS the fixture string count as \"represented\", with no manifest\nand no proof kind - and with an item of an unrelated kind. This directly contradicts oracle.py's own\ndocstring.\n\nRequired repair: a negative fixture is represented ONLY through a plan-level declaration that binds the\nfixture to a proof KIND which is actually present in the checked evidence. Delete the bare\n`fixture in present_ids` fallback entirely. An item cannot supply its own representation through any\ncaller-chosen field (`item_id`, `negative_fixtures`, `negative_cases`, or anything else).\nAdd tests: (a) item_id == fixture with no manifest -> `NEGATIVE_FIXTURE_UNREPRESENTED`; (b) item of an\nunrelated kind named the fixture, plus a real item, -> still unreprsented; (c) item self-declaring\n`negative_fixtures`/`negative_cases` -> unreprsented; (d) a genuine plan-level manifest binding the\nfixture to a present proof kind -> represented and the oracle may pass.\n\n## F2 — `src/effect/idempotency.py` + `substrate.py` + `README.md`: PARTIAL_EFFECT must not be retried\n\n`plan_retry` currently allows a retry from `PARTIAL_EFFECT`, re-attempting a partially-applied effect\nand discarding its readbacks. `src/effect/README.md` says uncertainty is answered with a fresh readback\nrather than another side effect.\n\nRequired repair: retry is allowed ONLY from `UNKNOWN_EFFECT` (where no effect has been confirmed\napplied). `PARTIAL_EFFECT` is NOT retryable: `plan_retry` returns `allowed=False` with\n`reason_code=\"RETRY_REFUSED_PARTIAL_EFFECT\"` and `assert_retryable` raises `RetryRefused`; the\nrecovery route for a partial effect is a fresh readback (`plan_reobserve`) plus the compensation\npointer. Make the README, the docstrings and the code agree. Keep retry REACHABLE end-to-end from\n`UNKNOWN_EFFECT` through the public API. Add tests for both the refusal and the still-working\nUNKNOWN_EFFECT retry path.\n\n## F3 — `src/security/classification.py`: the hard gate ignores bytes\n\n`classify(b\"...\")` already fail-closes to `SECRET` for a non-str value, but `assert_no_secret()` does\nnot raise and `sanitize_evidence()` leaves a bytes-encoded credential in place with `clean=True`.\n\nRequired repair: any `bytes`/`bytearray` scalar anywhere in the payload is unscannable and therefore\nfail-closed: `assert_no_secret` raises `SecretExfiltrationBlocked`, and `sanitize_evidence` replaces\nthe scalar with a marker (e.g. `[REDACTED:UNSCANNABLE_BYTES]`) and reports `clean=False` with an\n`unscannable_bytes` count. Do NOT start flagging ordinary scalars (`int`, `float`, `bool`, `None`) -\nthose are not credentials and flagging them would break every event payload. Add tests for both\ndirections.\n\n## F4 — `src/assurance/evidence.py`: the security axis must discriminate like every other axis\n\nThe reviewer showed that any `security_config` change invalidates EVERY gate (including a gate bound to\nthe NEW config and a gate with no security binding), contradicting the `_superseded()` promise that\n\"the same rule is used for every axis\".\n\nRequired repair: use the SAME discriminating rule on the security axis: a gate is invalidated when the\nidentity it was bound to is no longer the current one, and a gate with no binding for that axis is not\ninvalidated by that axis. Add tests: superseded security binding invalidated; current security binding\nuntouched; unbound gate untouched. Keep the fail-safe property that a gate carrying the OLD config is\nnever treated as current.\n\n## F5 — `src/assurance/journal.py`: label the unauthenticated header honestly and anchor on the manifest\n\nThe reviewer removed the last entry and coherently rewrote `header.entry_count` and\n`header.final_digest`; `verify()` then reported INTACT. Without key management a fully coherent rewrite\nis genuinely undetectable by the header alone - the honest repair is to say so and make the manifest\nthe anchor.\n\nRequired repair:\n1. `verify()` keeps detecting the header-inconsistent cases (SEQ_GAP, HEADER_MISMATCH, ...) but its\n   result MUST carry `header_is_authoritative: false` and a `reason_code`/field stating that a\n   coherent header+entry rewrite is not detectable without an external anchor.\n2. Add a first-class `verify_against_manifest(manifest)` (or equivalent) that IS authoritative and\n   detects the truncation (`ENTRY_DIGEST_MISMATCH` / count mismatch).\n3. `threat_assessment()` must state plainly: detection only, no signature, no key management, the\n   header is not authoritative, the manifest is the anchor, and a coherent rewrite of both the entries\n   and the unauthenticated header is undetectable - do not claim otherwise.\n4. Add a test that reproduces the reviewer's exact attack and asserts `verify()` no longer reports an\n   unqualified INTACT (it must surface the non-authoritative header) while\n   `verify_against_manifest(retained_manifest)` catches the truncation.\n\n## Definition of done\n\nAll three affected roots must pass with counts strictly GREATER than 177 / 100 / 116:\n\n```\npython -m unittest discover -s src/security/tests    -t src/security/tests\npython -m unittest discover -s src/effect/tests      -t src/effect/tests\npython -m unittest discover -s src/assurance/tests   -t src/assurance/tests\n```\n\nPrint a JSON object when finished: `{\"files\": [...], \"counts\": {\"security\": N, \"effect\": N, \"assurance\": N}}`.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
